Z||000000||Fierokid87||12-25-2001||10:51 PM||||Hey all if you can send me any pictures and info one the routing and what size goes to what plug for the plug wires I would greatly apreciate it.  Thanks<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-26-2001||10:42 AM||||You can route them anyway you want, as long as they are away from heat and look neat.  Stock wire sizes are 7mm, most people get 8mm or 8.8mm high performance wires.  Different colors are available as well.  Try summit or autozone even, they can get a nice set of Accel 8.8mm (yellow) ones that come pre cut for the Fiero V6.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kasdan||12-26-2001||12:38 PM||||i use the bosch premium wires, got them at autozone, think they were like 30 or 40 bucks maybe?  oh well, they work great for me<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierokid87||12-26-2001||03:40 PM||||I have a bit of a nack for having the plug wires routed differently.  Also I have a set of the STI factory red wires.  I kinda want the wires routed how they were from the factory.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||12-26-2001||03:46 PM||||I'll snap a pic of my 16K mile '88 GT's engine compartment for you in a minute (still has original wires and original routing).<P>Just so you know.....there are only 3 different sizes of plug wires on the V-6......2 short, 2 long and 2 in between. <P>The short ones go to the plugs that are closest to the distributor (cyl #5 & #6), the middle sized wires go to the middle cylinders (#3 & #4) and the two longest wires go to cylinders #1 & #2 (closest to teh passenger side of the car).<P>Give me a few minutes to snap and load a pic.<P>   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||12-26-2001||04:12 PM||||Here we go......pardon how dirty the engine is, I haven't driven/cleaned it since last spring!<P>LMK if these help or if you want me to take different angles. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Im000333.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Im000330.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Im000329.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pyric||12-26-2001||04:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>You can route them anyway you want, as long as they are away from heat and look neat.  Stock wire sizes are 7mm, most people get 8mm or 8.8mm high performance wires.  Different colors are available as well.  Try summit or autozone even, they can get a nice set of Accel 8.8mm (yellow) ones that come pre cut for the Fiero V6.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey!  My factory manual says the 85 v6 had 8mm stock.  but all the parts places give you 7mm as stock replacements.  <P>Anyone else notice that?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||12-26-2001||04:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pyric:<BR><B> Hey!  My factory manual says the 85 v6 had 8mm stock.  but all the parts places give you 7mm as stock replacements.  <P>Anyone else notice that?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I've never noticed that, of course I don't own an '85 Fiero!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>As you can see from my pics, the factory Packard wires were 7mm (same as all '85-'88 V-6 Fieros).<BR>||||reg||1
